s been  and it is incredibly harmful and  dangerous and is factually incorrect  because the the story that we hear is  that 11 million immigrants are the  reason and the source of all of our  country's problems and that if we just  get rid of them  that there will be no more problems in  America and of course I couldn't be  further from the truth and in fact when  I think about immigrants and why we come  here I always I always have this thought  in my mind that immigrants are willing  to risk their very lives they are  willing to cross oceans and  walk-throughs asserts and leave  everything behind because that's how  much they believe in America that's how  much they believe that they can come to  this country in search of a better life  and if we wanted to just get by and get  on welfare as many people believe we  would have just stayed where we were  that's not why we come here and getting  rid of 11 million people it's not only  the humanizing rhetoric but when you  think about just from an economic  standpoint if from one day to the next  your population shrinks by 11 million  people and 11 million people don't go to  work tomorrow an 11 million people  aren't buying things and paying sales  taxes and creating economic activity  that is going to have a deep impact in  the economy of our country so not only  is deporting 11 million people not a  solution it actually would create  significant economic problems for  Americans well  jalisa this has been an amazing time to  spend with you very very best wishes and  thank you so much for writing this book  about your story thank you so much for  having me
 

